      "item": "thm-bipolar-closure-for-linear-subspaces",
      "finding": "The Statement asserts 'For a linear subspace M <= X, the primal formula is ^perp(M^perp) = closure M^{norm}' with no HB or AC hypothesis, but with M = 0 that formula says X* separates points of X, which the library records only under HB in cor-relative-hahn-banach-dual-norming ('Assume HB ... Hence X* separates distinct points'). The proof itself reaches it through F4 cor-annihilator-detects-closure, whose proof cites thm-geometric-hahn-banach-for-subspaces, which cites thm-norm-preserving-extension-from-any-subspace, which cites thm-hahn-banach-norm-preserving-extension and thm-complex-hahn-banach-norm-preserving-extension, which cite thm-hahn-banach-dominated-extension, whose Statement begins 'Assume the Axiom of Choice'. So an assumption used in the proof chain is not restated in the statement (the same is true of cor-annihilator-detects-closure, thm-geometric-hahn-banach-for-subspaces, thm-norm-preserving-extension-from-any-subspace and the analytic-page consumers), contrary to the convention stated in def-hahn-banach-extension-principle-relative ('Subsequent results explicitly state when they assume HB'). The weak-star identity in the same item is genuinely ZF and is the only part used by lem-annihilators-are-weak-and-weak-star-closed.",
      "severity": "gap-a-reader-closes"
    }
  ],
